# Context & Skills Workflow

## Authority (when docs conflict)

1. User's explicit request in chat
2. `AGENTS.md` — stack, invariants, folder layout
3. `context/IDEA.md` — product truth (what to build)
4. `context/progress-tracker.md` — what's done and what's next
5. `docs/superpowers/specs/` — phase specs (e.g. UI shell)
6. Other `context/` files — how to build
7. General training knowledge — last resort; verify against `package.json`

## Context read order by task

| Task | Read first |
|---|---|
| Any work | `progress-tracker.md` |
| New feature / module | `IDEA.md` → relevant roadmap/spec → `project-overview.md` → `architecture.md` |
| UI component | `ui-registry.md` → `ui-rules.md` → `ui-tokens.md` |
| Store / state | `architecture.md` (card model) → `code-standards.md` (Zustand) |
| New dependency | `code-standards.md` (Dependencies) — update list before installing |
| Library API | `library-docs.md` → `AGENTS.md` |

Do not assume. If `progress-tracker.md` or specs contradict memory, trust the files.

## Project skills (`.cursor/skills/`)

Invoke by reading the skill file before acting — never skip when it applies.

| Skill | When |
|---|---|
| **architect** | Before any non-trivial feature — plan + confirm before code |
| **imprint** | After every new UI component — update `context/ui-registry.md` |
| **review** | After a feature is built — verify against plan, architecture, UI rules |
| **remember save** | End of session — hand off state for next session |
| **remember restore** | Start of session — restore prior context |
| **recover** | Build went wrong — diagnose failure type before more prompting |
| **grill-me** | User wants to stress-test a plan or design |

Superpowers skills (brainstorming, TDD, verification-before-completion, etc.) apply when relevant — check skill descriptions; brainstorming before creative work, verification before claiming done.

## Standard workflows

**New feature:** `progress-tracker` → `architect` → read context above → implement → `imprint` (if UI) → `review` → update `progress-tracker` → `npm run lint`

**Bug fix:** read affected area in `architecture.md` → fix minimally → `npm run lint`

**Session end:** update `progress-tracker.md` if status changed → `/remember save`

## Context maintenance

When you change stack, dependencies, architecture, or UI patterns — update the matching `context/` file in the same session. Never leave context stale after a structural change.

**Do not** duplicate `AGENTS.md` or full context files in chat — cite paths and read what you need.
